build: 2026-06-20 v10.34.10 (full-app sweep — metering/export hardening + UI consistency)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
includes: Follow-up to v10.34.9's stability pass, from a full-app audit (UI/design, code-quality, brand/claims). (1) True-peak meter now keeps separate signed inter-sample history per channel — it previously fed the Catmull-Rom interpolator the channel-linked rectified value mixed with a signed sample, skewing the reading (metering only, no effect on audio output). (2) Audio export (loudness scan + gain apply) now walks CMBlockBuffer segments by offset instead of reading/writing totalLength/4 from a single data pointer — closes a theoretical out-of-bounds read/write on a segmented block (behaviour-identical for the usual single-segment LPCM buffer). (3) Onboarding screen is now themed on EchoelTheme (off-white #e0e0e0 text, Atkinson Hyperlegible font with Dynamic Type + pinch-zoom, the documented monochrome primary-button pattern) so it shares one visual language with the app and echoelmusic.com — it previously used hardcoded white/black + system fonts. (4) Brand cleanup: removed a legacy "soundscape" docstring and unused esoteric-named ("quantum"/"wellness") log categories. Code-quality sweep of Studio/Views/Tools/Core/Sync came back clean. Verified: ci.yml (build+test, all platforms) + xcode-compile-check (AUv3 included) green on e8f98b4. Plus everything from v10.34.3–v10.34.9.
